# SkillMD Research: Best Audited Skills for Planning, Coding & Linux Admin

**Date:** 2026-10-23
**Source:** SkillMD registry via MCP (`https://api.skillmd.com/mcp`), 860,000+ indexed SKILL.md files
**Method:** 40+ targeted `skillmd_search` queries + `skillmd_trending` + `skillmd_get` on 42 shortlisted skills.
**Filter:** Only skills with `ai_audit_verdict = pass` and `audits_passed = 3` were treated as "best audited."

> **Important caveat about this install:** the MCP server itself works perfectly, but
> `claudio-backend/src/claudio_backend/supervisor.py:176` (`_warn_if_mcp_configured`)
> states the current ADK engine **does not load MCP tools**. All SkillMD access in this
> research was done by calling the streamable-HTTP JSON-RPC endpoint directly
> (`smd.py`), not through the agent's tool chain.

---

## How SkillMD scores a skill

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `ai_audit_verdict` | `pass` / `caution` / `warning` / `fail` / `inconclusive` |
| `audits_passed` | Number of audit passes (3 = fully audited) |
| `security_flags` | `docs_only`, `network_calls`, `executes_scripts`, `reads_secrets`, `untrusted_install` |
| `craft_score` | Quality of the skill writing itself (0-100) |
| `repo_stars` | GitHub stars of the upstream source repo (popularity proxy) |
| `avg_rating` | Community rating (0-5) |
| `commit_sha` | Pinned upstream commit (supply-chain provenance) |

**Key finding:** 213 of the ~558 skills surfaced across all queries had `pass` + 3 audits.
Popularity and craft are only weakly correlated — some of the best-written skills
(craft 90-100) come from tiny repos with no stars, while some mega-star repos ship
thin, generic skills. The rankings below weight **audit status and craft first, stars second.**


